Parent: The given text is a detailed explanation of three problems related to ranking and retrieval queries on datasets, specifically focusing on Parent-Child relationships in the context of data structures and algorithms within computer science. These problems are part of a larger discussion about efficient methods for finding specific ranked points or sets of points based on scoring functions applied to attributes (features) within a dataset. The first problem focuses on retrieving a single point at a given rank, while the second introduces a relaxed version that returns a set containing all possible conformal points. The third problem extends this concept by defining and solving for a stripe range query which involves finding all data points within certain score boundaries.
[all_together_subsections] parent=Formal Definitions sample=3 attempt=3/5
